# Prettier 3 reads .gitignore by default, so dist/, storybook-static/,
# coverage/, playwright-report/, test-results/ and every locale but en are
# already out of scope. This file is only for what is committed and must
# still not be reformatted.

# Machine-generated, and Prettier corrupts it. pnpm writes package keys that
# exceed YAML's 1024-character implicit-key limit in explicit-key form
# (`? '<key>'` on one line, `: ` on the next); Prettier rewrites them as
# ordinary `"<key>":` mappings, which is invalid YAML. pnpm then reports
# "Ignoring broken lockfile", discards it and re-resolves every dependency --
# and CI's --frozen-lockfile fails outright.
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Derived from a DocSpace client checkout by `pnpm sync-locales`
# (scripts/copy-locales.js). Both are committed so the package builds and runs
# Storybook standalone, but they are copies: formatting them here only creates
# drift that the next sync silently reverts.
locales/
css/

# Prettier's Markdown printer escapes `*` inside the `{/* ... */}` expression
# that opens every component doc with the licence header -- it emits `{/\*`
# and `\*/}`, which is no longer a JavaScript comment. Storybook's indexer then
# fails every one of those files with "Could not parse expression with acorn"
# and refuses to start at all. It broke 18 files the first time `pnpm format`
# ran here, and nothing before Storybook itself would have caught it.
*.mdx
